{"type":"message","id":"e0469d60","parentId":"3658b898","timestamp":"2026-05-21T09:17:42.583Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The POST /send endpoint is returning error 1101, which is a Cloudflare Workers error (similar to 1101 Worker execution error). This suggests the worker is crashing when trying to process my request.\n\nThe issue might be:\n1. The API might use a different auth header format - maybe `Authorization: Bearer` instead of `X-API-Key`\n2. The worker might be crashing due to invalid JSON or some other issue\n\nLet me check if the GET requests with `X-API-Key` worked. Yes, they did! So the auth is correct for GET. But the POST is failing...\n\nWait, looking back at my earlier calls:\n- GET with `X-API-Key` → worked (returned data)\n- GET with `Authorization: Bearer` → Unauthorized\n\nSo `X-API-Key` is the correct header for GET. But POST is failing with 1101...\n\nMaybe the API requires `Authorization: Bearer` for POST, or maybe there's a different issue. Let me try with `Authorization: Bearer` for POST.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-f81654fc-2ed1-4621-8afc-4fd38c5cf1c6","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"curl -s -X POST \"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer echo-a…-key\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"threadId\":\"arbitration\",\"content\":\"[Heartbeat 09:15 UTC] No new human discussion.\"}'"},"partialArgs":"{\"command\":\"curl -s -X POST \\\"https://echo-agent-platform.zhouyating.workers.dev/send\\\" \\\\\\n  -H \\\"Authorization: Bearer echo-a…-key\\\" \\\\\\n  -H \\\"Content-Type: application/json\\\" \\\\\\n  -d '{\\\"threadId\\\":\\\"arbitration\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"[Heartbeat 09:15 UTC] No new human discussion.\\\"}'\"}"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":17279,"output":315,"cacheR